		(uuid "02974a0c-3b8e-57db-bf0f-e29d37d9e813")
	)
	(text
		"J_SWD pin1 +3V3, pin2 SWDIO, pin3 GND, pin4 SWCLK, pin5 NRST. No USB bootloader; program over SWD."
		(at 17.59 146.065 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "75254d0a-5805-519d-a725-c5b310f10383")
	)
	(text
		"LSE 32.768 kHz on PC14/PC15 (OSC32_IN/OSC32_OUT): the LQFP-32 STM32G030K8 has no HSE crystal oscillator (HSE runs only in bypass mode), so the system clock is HSI16 and the crystal feeds the RTC. Crystal Epson FC-135 32.7680KF-AG0 (LCSC C7275974), CL 7 pF, R1 70 kOhm typ, C0 1.0 pF typ (Epson FC-135 datasheet Ver 2.0). CL = (C1 x C2)/(C1 + C2) + Cstray with Cstray 5 pF, so C1 = C2 = 2 x (7 - 5) = 4 pF. Nearest standard value (E24) 4.3 pF: CL = 4.3/2 + 5 = 7.15 pF, 0.15 pF from 7 pF. Cstray 5 pF is an assumption, not measured. Crystal critical transconductance gm_crit = 4 x R1 x (2 pi f)^2 x (C0 + CL)^2 = 4 x 70 kOhm x (2.059e5)^2 x (8.15 pF)^2 = 0.79 uA/V; DS12991 gives a maximum crystal Gm_crit of 0.5, 0.75, 1.7 and 2.7 uA/V for LSEDRV low, medium low, medium high and high (as relayed in the maintainer review; the datasheet itself was not retrieved here), which already carry the safety margin, so 0.79 uA/V needs LSEDRV medium high (1.7 uA/V). The 70 kOhm ESR is the Epson datasheet's typical value and the LCSC listing's figure; the datasheet states no maximum."
		(at 17.59 148.605 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "84075920-a87f-584d-a03f-b3f9d3f33c29")
	)
	(text
		"Boot: PA14 (SWCLK) is BOOT0; default option bytes boot from flash."
		(at 17.59 151.145 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c4dd30b9-4bd1-59a4-bf62-ef76d43604fc")
	)
